more than half of the residents in a  henderson nursing home contracted coping  19  according to the state's covet 19  dashboard now out of the reported 104  residents with the virus  29 died it's a story the i-team has been  following about  outbreaks inside of nursing homes and  now the granddaughter of a woman who  passed away says she wants answers  after her family was kept in the dark  the i-team's vanessa murphy is in studio  tonight with what she learned about this  case vanessa  denise yesterday would have been maxine  williams 90th  birthday her granddaughter says she  understands there was a pandemic and  people are going to catch covid19 but  she has questions about how the nursing  home where her grandmother lived  handled the situation  my grandmother died alone in the  hospital  maxine williams died of covid19  according to her death certificate  erin jones says her 89 year old  grandmother had dementia and was a  resident  at del mar gardens in henderson on july  17  her family received a call that williams  was taken to a hospital by ambulance  no one at the facility knew anything  they didn't know what hospital she went  to all they could tell us  she went by ambulance to a hospital  after several calls  jones says she was able to confirm her  grandmother was taken to saint rose  dominican hospital's  siena campus where she died they sent  her to the hospital  on a friday afternoon and she passed  away in the emergency room a couple  hours later she didn't make it to be  admitted  jones has questions about the days  leading up to her grandmother's death  the i-team examined 130 pages of medical  records that her family says they  obtained from del mar gardens  on july 8 williams had a cough and was  prescribed medicine  on july 13 she was tested for covid 19.  the cough was on and off through the  15th on the 16th  test results came back positive for the  virus  by then williams had a low-grade fever  she was given a nasal cannula for help  breathing  and records show she was so  uncomfortable she was moaning  on the 17th her oxygen level dropped to  75  medical staff noted that 90 to 100 is  normal  that's when an ambulance was called  how did they get that bad according to  these records staff reached out to the  family  six times over the course of the nine  days to provide updates  but the family disputes that jones also  says the family was  not allowed to communicate with williams  by phone or  face time as requested there was  something going on they were telling us  about  the attending physician identified in  medical records is dr  charles mcswain it is unclear from those  records whether he examined williams in  person before she was taken to the  hospital  when reached by phone dr mcswain told  the i-team  during that time he was not making  regular visits  and declined to comment further the  i-team also obtained state inspection  records for del mar gardens  the month williams died of the virus  there was one violation with at least  six different components according to  the department of health and human  services  this report dated july first states the  facility did not have sufficient  infection prevention and control  it is noted one resident who was being  monitored due to a fever and cough  was in a room with a resident who had no  covet 19 symptoms  their beds two feet apart the report  also noted  disinfectant cleaner not being used  properly  and laundry staff not wearing proper  personal protective equipment or ppe  in hindsight it kind of felt like she  didn't really have a chance to not get  infected  by august 13th del mar gardens provided  retraining and made changes to address  the deficiencies according to this  document  no deficiencies were found in two  additional visits  as of february 19th the state reports  58 percent of residents contracted covid  19  29 of them died i just want someone to  be held responsible  i reached out to del mar gardens i  called the nursing home 